{
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": "05:00",
      "text": "selves all the time."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:01",
      "text": "We try to force ourselves to try harder instead of learning a different skill."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:05",
      "text": "So, if you want to stop being so reactive, you've got to build muscle memory for a bunch of new tiny skills."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:12",
      "text": "It's it's the same for learning to shoot a basketball or be more patient or be more assertive."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:18",
      "text": "You have to break it down into tiny steps and then practice each one until you're good at it and then put all the pieces together."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:24",
      "text": "And to do this, you need proper technique, visual aids, often coaching, and then with a bit of practice, you'll build the muscle memory to be able to do it even under pressure."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:33",
      "text": "So, you can't just try harder."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:37",
      "text": "That's the first principle."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:38",
      "text": "Willpower doesn't work, okay?"
    },
    {
      "start": "05:40",
      "text": "You've got to train some new reflexes."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:42",
      "text": "And the way you do that is through practicing tiny skills."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:45",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:46",
      "text": "Second principle is that our brains do not comprehend don't do that."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:51",
      "text": "When we try to be less impulsive, that's called a negative goal because it's something you're trying to subtract."
    },
    {
      "start": "05:57",
      "text": "The brain doesn't know what to do with negative goals."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:00",
      "text": "There's no action there, there's no verb."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:02",
      "text": "So principle two for being less impulsive is stop it is less effective than do this instead."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:09",
      "text": "You have to train yourself to do a different action."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:12",
      "text": "You can see this with toddlers."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:14",
      "text": "If you tell them don't hit the cat, they have no idea what you're telling them to do."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:19",
      "text": "The only action word there is hit and their developing brain just can't process the don't in front of it."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:26",
      "text": "It can't process that negative word."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:27",
      "text": "A toddler does much better when you tell them what to do."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:31",
      "text": "So you say something like, use soft hands with the cat."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:36",
      "text": "Here, let me show you."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:38",
      "text": "Now, we adults aren't much different."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:40",
      "text": "Our brains are not that that different."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:42",
      "text": "When we want to be less impulsive, we have to give our brain an action word."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:46",
      "text": "What are we doing instead?"
    },
    {
      "start": "06:49",
      "text": "So, here's a quick example."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:50",
      "text": "When people train adults who have a tendency to hit their kids, when they train them, they don't tell them to stop hitting their kids."
    },
    {
      "start": "06:58",
      "text": "They tell them to replace that behavior"
    }
  ]
}
